To print the elements of an `ArrayList` in Java, you can use a for-each loop or a regular for loop.

Using for-each loop:
```java
ArrayList<String> myList = new ArrayList<>();
myList.add("apple");
myList.add("banana");
myList.add("orange");

for (String element : myList) {
    System.out.println(element);
}
```
Output:
```
apple
banana
orange
```
Using regular for loop:
```java
ArrayList<String> myList = new ArrayList<>();
myList.add("apple");
myList.add("banana");
myList.add("orange");

for (int i = 0; i < myList.size(); i++) {
    System.out.println(myList.get(i));
}
```
Output:
```
apple
